\begin{equation*}
\phi\mu^{2}S+\rho\mu S+\phi\sigma_{x}^{2}\Big[\,1+c\,(S-1)\Big]=0 ,
\end{equation*}
i.e.

\begin{equation*}
1+c\,(S-1)=-
\frac{\mu^{2}+\rho\mu/\phi}{\sigma_{x}^{2}}\,S\equiv\kappa_{*}S .
\end{equation*}
Hence the marginal stability point can be written in the canonical
form

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{*}S-1}{S-1},
\qquad 
\kappa_{*}:=-
\frac{\mu^{2}+\rho\mu/\phi}{\sigma_{x}^{2}}
=-\,\frac{\mu\big(\phi\mu+\rho\big)}{\phi\,\sigma_{x}^{2}}\;,
\end{equation*}
the dimensionless Hebbian–homeostatic control parameter.  In the
rate normalisation normally used in the literature
${\rm Cov}(x_{k},x_{l})=\mu^{2}c_{kl}$, $\sigma_{x}^{2}=\mu^{2}$, so that

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{*}=-\,\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
=-1-\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\ ,
\qquad 
c^{*}(S)=\frac{-\,S\big[1+\rho/\phi\mu\big]-1}{S-1},
\end{equation*}
and $\lim_{S\to\infty}c^{*}=\kappa_{*}$.  Up to the inessential overall
sign which is absorbed in the convention for the additive offset the
parameter which is normally quoted is

\begin{equation*}
\hat\kappa:=-\kappa_{*}=1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}
          =\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}\;,
\end{equation*}
